This note provides further explanation for key components of the Drinfeld-Langlands program as outlined in Gaitonde and Langlands' paper [1], specifically focusing on their initial framework and its connections to Drinfeld's conjecture about the kernel $K_3$. By doing so, these concepts are linked to the broader geometric Langlands program under certain conditions, particularly in the genus-zero case. An appendix provides a simplified proof of Drinfeld's conjecture about $K_3$ for the case of a curve of genus one. The main text also explores an extension of Drinfeld-Langlands' program to incorporate $\mathrm{GSp}(2)$ and $\mathrm{GO}$-type groups, leading to an analogous program for a specific group. An additional consequence of this work is the derivation of a formula connecting the local L-function of a rank one vector space to its functional equation. This relationship mirrors a formula previously established by Bump and Ginzburg in the case of a reductive group. An alternative proof of Drinfeld-Langlands' conjecture for $\mathrm{GSp}(2)$ is also offered, utilizing the same strategy of combining the local Langlands program with the geometric Langlands program. The appendix and main text are distinct entities that were initially written independently, leading to some duplication of information. As a result, some arguments in the main text are presented in duplicate, and readers may choose to read either section to understand the content. The author is grateful to the anonymous referee for pointing out a crucial error in the original version of the paper, leading to the correction of this issue. The author is also grateful to the support of the Simons Foundation ( award number 984271) in the completion of this work. \bigskip

